 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwave not working"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "A microwave that appears 'not working' usually stems from one of three areas: the power supply reaching the unit, a control lock preventing operation, or a safety interlock (door switch) stopping it from starting. Please check the following:\n1. Power: Ensure the plug is firmly in the socket and the socket is switched on. If your microwave has a digital display, does it light up when plugged in?\n2. Door: Does the door close smoothly and latch securely? Some microwaves will not start if the door isn't fully engaged. Once you've checked these, let me know what happens."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "yes the display is on, shows the time. door closes fine. buttons just beep and nothing starts"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since the display is on and the door closes properly, but the buttons only beep without starting, this often points to a control lock being active or a keypad issue. Many microwaves have a 'Child Lock' feature that prevents operation; look for a key or padlock symbol on the display. Try holding the 'Stop' button for 3-5 seconds to see if it unlocks. If there is no lock icon and it still won't start, please find the model number (usually inside the door frame or on the back) so I can give you specific steps.\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "there's a little L symbol on the display. will try holding stop for 3 secs"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That 'L' symbol suggests the Child Lock was active. Please go ahead and try holding the Stop button for 3-5 seconds as you planned. If that clears the lock and it starts working again, you're all set—just remember how to unlock it next time if it happens again. However, if the 'L' stays on or it still won't start even after unlocking, I'll need to know exactly which model it is to guide you further. Could you please tell me the brand and model number (usually found on a sticker inside the door frame or on the back of the unit)?\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok just held stop for 3 secs, the L has gone and it works now"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news! It was simply the child lock being active. To avoid this happening again in future, just remember that holding the Stop button for a few seconds will toggle it on or off. Is there anything else I can help you with today?\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  }
 ],
